{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing edge into the output with a conv restores connectivity and adds a learnable path, a bigger gain than replacing skip or pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty direct input-to-output edge with a conv adds more than upgrading an existing skip connection."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Edge 0 feeds node 1, so restoring it from none to conv gives a large gain over replacing skip or pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to a missing intermediate edge creates a deeper path, which helps more than replacing a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring the edge into node 2 with a conv helps more than swapping one existing op for another."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none with conv adds a new learnable route into the output, a larger gain than replacing a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a conv on the input edge costs far more accuracy than removing a weak op such as pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv with pooling loses learnable capacity, whereas replacing a skip or none loses little or gains."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading the dir